id: pm-slack-standup-commitment-variance
title: Compare selected standup commitments with revision-cited outcomes and scope changes
description: ""
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-29T06:33:18.844Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-29T07:04:57.114Z"
author: codex-agent
comments[7]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-29T06:33:21.881Z",codex-agent,"Overlap rechecked against core command/source search and sibling README contracts: core owns native history, statuses and relationship reads; pm-brief owns acknowledged handoff contracts; pm-slack owns delivery acknowledgments; prior impediment acknowledgments remain separate. This feature compares explicitly selected periodic intent with linked outcome evidence and later scope changes; it assigns no work and sends no reminders. Existing progress deltas supply evidence inspection and verified history. No matching package or core issue was found by commitment variance search."
  "2026-10-29T06:35:09.915Z",codex-agent,"Design: read-only selected source revision with per-comment standup-commitment/v1 declarations. Each declaration binds a key to a native target revision; malformed/foreign annotations are isolated. SDK replay and verified history provide baselines, full intervening scope changes (including ABA), outcome revisions and role-based lifecycle meaning. Report carries no bodies and covers up to twenty keys. No capture/write/import/sync journal is introduced; native comments remain the supported capture mechanism. Re-read source, target and settings witnesses before returning, refusing detected interleaving; a peer can still change state after its final check, and no workspace transaction isolation is claimed (core #1620)."
  "2026-10-29T06:43:49.612Z",codex-agent,"First focused run: 5/8 passed. Three test expectations exposed SDK contracts: canonical body trimming, schema definitions stored separately from settings, and lossless TOON table JSON-column metadata. Adjusted the assertions to use SDK historical reads and decodePmTableRows; custom empty-role statuses now remain unsupported. The twenty-commitment large-body fixture measured 6561 JSON bytes. Added an SDK-backed seeded state model with older-input replays, CRLF variants, all inspected native scope fields, revision binding, random custom role registries and ambient focus."
  "2026-10-29T06:53:21.504Z",codex-agent,"Public-data validation passed against public main 83f4e1ee5d2fde97254c6fa8044f5cc017314691: 107 certified items, 107 reports, 1048 native events, 107 missing captures, 252 foreign comments, zero declared commitments, invalid annotations or refusals, and 220/220 files unchanged (bytes, names, modes and mtimes) with git absent. The twenty explicitly missing-key control returned 20 unsupported rows in 2967 JSON bytes; this is absence evidence, not positive outcome prevalence. Lint/typecheck/docstrings and zero-duplication checks run locally; full release gates remain assigned to CI."
  "2026-10-29T07:00:54.051Z",codex-agent,"Validation passed: focused commitment suite 10/10; both new runtime modules measured 100% statements, branches, functions and lines. The independent SDK state model passed 500 sequences with 3363 native mutations across eight generated custom registries, zero mismatches, older-input/CRLF replays and all inspected native scope fields. Four disposable changed-function reverts (scope detection, target revision binding, missing-capture uncertainty, read-witness validation) each failed an assertion; restored production code passed the three selected regressions. The package worktree was never behaviorally mutated. SDK settings metadata is used to refuse unavailable configuration instead of silently interpreting fallback defaults; legacy format warnings remain readable."
  "2026-10-29T07:01:50.226Z",codex-agent,"Linked native test execution passed 1/1 commands and 10/10 tests. Existing tracker policy disables automatic test-result persistence; no setting was changed. CI will run the unchanged npm and Bun release gates, including the 500-sequence model and all six packed scenarios (npm/Bun current and minimum via npx/bunx plus true npm and Bun global hosts). No import/export/sync writers, native mutation journals or shared package leases are introduced. Remaining concurrency window: a peer may update a previously rechecked stream before other checks finish or after return; observed revisions remain explicit and no atomic snapshot is promised."
  "2026-10-29T07:04:57.113Z",codex-agent,"Ready-for-review PR: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-slack-standup/pull/166 . Initial CI run: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-slack-standup/actions/runs/40833074136 . This final tracker handoff will trigger a fresh exact-head run; the PR records its final URL and gate counts. Tracker history integrity passes. Local default health initially refused an inherited global pm-github host-version skew (pinned SDK 2026.10.25 versus extension host 2026.10.28); strict health passes with an isolated global path and extensions disabled, matching clean-checkout isolation. Existing provenance and telemetry advisories remain advisory; no history rewrite, SDK pin bump or telemetry configuration change was made. Item remains unclosed and released for orchestrator verification."
